%S A400385 1,2,0,12,0,7200,766080,151603200,48990735360,28946545689600,
%T A400385 32147584690636800,69035747184817459200,290738883045236161536000
%N A400385 Number of labeled simple graphs on [n] whose automorphism group acts semiregularly on the vertices.
%C A400385 Equivalently, no nonidentity automorphism of the graph fixes a vertex.
%C A400385 The graphs with trivial automorphism group form a subclass counted by n!*A003400(n) = A330343(n).
%H A400385 J.-L. Du, Y.-Q. Feng and P. Spiga, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcta.2019.105174">A classification of the graphical m-semiregular representation of finite groups</a>, J. Combin. Theory Ser. A 171 (2020), 105174.
%F A400385 Let o_2(H) be the number of orbits of H <= S_n on the 2-subsets of [n], and let mu be the Möbius function of the subgroup lattice of S_n. Then a(n) = Sum_{H semiregular} Sum_{K >= H} mu(H,K)*2^o_2(K), where the outer sum is over all subgroups H <= S_n such that no nonidentity element of H fixes a point of [n].
%F A400385 For an odd prime p, a(p) = p!*A003400(p).
%e A400385 For n = 4, the 12 graphs counted are the labeled copies of the path P_4; hence a(4) = 4!/2 = 12.
%Y A400385 Cf. A003400 (unlabeled asymmetric graphs), A330343 (labeled asymmetric graphs).
%K A400385 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A400385 1,2
